# Checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# This is for a clone on a Windows machine, not for CI. Git for Windows
# installs with core.autocrlf=true, and test_all.sh does not survive the
# rewrite: a shebang line ending in a carriage return is not a shebang, and
# bash answers "env: bash\r: No such file or directory". A GitHub runner
# leaves the tree alone, so nothing here would have failed there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A skill tree is hashed, so git does not get to decide its bytes. Normalizing
# one silently changes a digest, and a fixture that wants a carriage return
# should keep it. Nothing in them has one today.
**/skills/** -text
**/testdata/** -text
